### Tira the Cafe Cat :smiley_cat:
Tira is a **CAT** owned by [vicelyav](https://github.com/vicelyav/ip)
Tira is based on a cat in my neighbourhood, whose behaviour can be summarised as:

> She is very fat - My Mom

This chatbot will help you:
* Add, delete, and modify your tasks
* Remember deadline and event timings
* Be a good cat friend

All you need to do is:
1. Follow the recommended task and date formatting
2. Remember to enter the correct command and update the task list
3. Say "bye" to end the chatbot to record your tasks

A short instruction on how to do this:
- [ ] Initialise Tira 
- [ ] Type your command
- [ ] To see your tasks, type list
- [ ] To end the chatbot, type "bye"

If you are a Java programmer, you can practice Java too. Here's a short snippet of the `main` class: 
``` ruby
public class Tira {
    private static final String Directory = "./data";
    private static final String FileName = "./data/Tira.txt";
    private static DateTimeFormatter IN_FORMATTER = DateTimeFormatter.ofPattern("yyyy-MM-dd");
    private Ui ui;
    private TaskList tasks;
    private Storage storage;
    private Parser parser;

    /**
     * Initialises the Tira class with the input filepath.
     * Loads task list from the file with the matching filename.
     *
     * @param filePath Filepath of the file to be updated.
     */

    public Tira(String filePath) {
        ui = new Ui();
        storage = new Storage(filePath);
        try {
            tasks = new TaskList(storage.load());
        } catch (TiraException e) {
            ui.showLoadingError();
            tasks = new TaskList();
        }
        parser = new Parser(tasks);

    } 
```

Tira's code is also designed to mimic a cat's behaviour, such as:
`     public void bye() {
        System.out.println("Bye. Come back with treats, MIAO!");
    } `
